{"name":"Rutabaga","hex":"#ead5b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rutabaga","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The swede, or Swedish turnip; the European plant Brassica napus var. napobrassica","The edible root of this plant"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rutabaga"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rutabaga","blocks":[{"text":"Rutabaga or swede is a root vegetable, a form of Brassica napus. Other names include Swedish turnip, neep (Scots), and turnip. However, elsewhere, the name turnip usually refers to the related white turnip."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Rutabaga%2C_variety_nadmorska.JPG/330px-Rutabaga%2C_variety_nadmorska.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rutabaga"},{"title":"Rutabaga (gene)","blocks":[{"text":"Rutabaga (rut) is the name of the gene encoding calcium-sensitive dependent adenylate cyclase in fruit flies.\nRutabaga has been implicated in a number of functions, including learning and memory, behavior, and cell communication. Its human homolog is ADCY1."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rutabaga_(gene)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Swede_-_rutabaga_-_veggiegroup.jpg/500px-Swede_-_rutabaga_-_veggiegroup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Swede_-_rutabaga_-_veggiegroup.jpg/500px-Swede_-_rutabaga_-_veggiegroup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Harvested roots","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwede_-_rutabaga_-_veggiegroup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bedegille.JPG/500px-Bedegille.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bedegille